  "content": {
    "id": "p2-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find the minimum perimeter of a rectangle formed using $40$ square tiles of side $1\\text{ cm}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$26\\text{ cm}$.\n\nThe $5\\text{ cm}\\times8\\text{ cm}$ arrangement has the smallest perimeter.",
      "worked": "The possible dimension pairs in centimetres are $(1,40)$, $(2,20)$, $(4,10)$ and $(5,8)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P_{1,40}&=2(1)+2(40)=82\\text{ cm}\\\\P_{2,20}&=2(2)+2(20)=44\\text{ cm}\\\\P_{4,10}&=2(4)+2(10)=28\\text{ cm}\\\\P_{5,8}&=2(5)+2(8)=26\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe minimum perimeter is $26\\text{ cm}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
